{
  "rationale": "The main idea is to check properties of the answer that must hold for any correct solution: the answer must be an integer between 1 and n (inclusive), must be consistent with trivial cases (n=1, all equal numbers), and must be at least the frequency of the most common element. Also, for small n (≤6) we can brute‑force the exact answer by checking all subsequences – this gives a definitive check. The tests are designed to be fast and rely only on the specification. The weakest test is test_max_one_subseq because it’s only a lower bound; if one had to drop a test, it would be that one.",
