  "rationale": "I will write tests that check basic properties of the output: shape, size, character set, symmetry, and the diamond pattern. All tests are derived directly from the specification. I will also compute the correct output by brute force for small n to catch any deviation. The tests are: 1) Output has exactly n lines. 2) Each line has exactly n characters. 3) Only '*' and 'D' appear. 4) The output is symmetric under top-bottom reversal. 5) The number of 'D's per row follows the diamond pattern. 6) The total number of 'D's equals the diamond area. 7) For n <= 11, compute the entire output by brute force and compare. 8) The middle row is all 'D's. 9) The outermost rows have exactly one 'D' in the middle. 10) The pattern of '*' and 'D' is consistent with the diamond definition: for each cell, check if it should be 'D' based on Manhattan distance from center. I would drop test 7 first if time constraints become an issue because it only covers small inputs, though it's a strong check.",
  "tests": [
    {
      "name": "test_line_count",
      "source": "def test_line_count(run, x):
    n = int(x.strip())
    out = run(x)
    lines = out.strip('\n').split('\n')
    assert len(lines) == n, f'Expected {n} lines, got {len(lines)}'"
    },
    {
      "name": "test_line_length",
      "source": "def test_line_length(run, x):
    n = int(x.strip())
    out = run(x)
    lines = out.strip('\n').split('\n')
    for i, line in enumerate(lines):
        assert len(line) == n, f'Line {i+1} length {len(line)} != {n}'"
    },
    {
      "name": "test_characters",
      "source": "def test_characters(run, x):
    out = run(x)
    lines = out.strip('\n').split('\n')
    for i, line in enumerate(lines):
        for ch in line:
            assert ch in '*D', f'Invalid character {ch} in line {i+1}'"
    },
    {
      "name": "test_top_bottom_symmetry",
      "source": "def test_top_bottom_symmetry(run, x):
    out = run(x)
    lines = out.strip('\n').split('\n')
    assert lines == lines[::-1], 'Output is not symmetric top-bottom'"
    },
    {
      "name": "test_diamond_row_counts",
      "source": "def test_diamond_row_counts(run, x):
    n = int(x.strip())
    out = run(x)
    lines = out.strip('\n').split('\n')
    for i, line in enumerate(lines):
        d_count = line.count('D')
        expected_d = n - 2 * abs(i - (n//2))
        assert d_count == expected_d, f'Row {i+1} has {d_count} D, expected {expected_d}'"
    },
    {
      "name": "test_total_d_count",
      "source": "def test_total_d_count(run, x):
    n = int(x.strip())
    out = run(x)
    lines = out.strip('\n').split('\n')
    total_d = sum(line.count('D') for line in lines)
    expected_total = n * n - 2 * ((n//2) * ((n//2)+1))  # area of diamond
    assert total_d == expected_total, f'Total D {total_d} != {expected_total}'"
    },
    {
      "name": "test_brute_force_small",
      "source": "def test_brute_force_small(run, x):
    n = int(x.strip())
    if n > 11:  # limit to keep fast
        return
    out = run(x)
    lines = out.strip('\n').split('\n')
    center = n // 2
    for i in range(n):
        expected_line = ''
        for j in range(n):
            if abs(i - center) + abs(j - center) <= center:
                expected_line += 'D'
            else:
                expected_line += '*'
        assert lines[i] == expected_line, f'Row {i+1} mismatch'"
    },
    {
      "name": "test_middle_row_all_d",
      "source": "def test_middle_row_all_d(run, x):
    n = int(x.strip())
    out = run(x)
    lines = out.strip('\n').split('\n')
    middle = lines[n//2]
    assert middle == 'D' * n, f'Middle row not all D: {middle}'"
    },
    {
      "name": "test_outer_rows_one_d",
      "source": "def test_outer_rows_one_d(run, x):
    n = int(x.strip())
    out = run(x)
    lines = out.strip('\n').split('\n')
    first = lines[0]
    last = lines[-1]
    expected = '*'*(n//2) + 'D' + '*'*(n//2)
    assert first == expected, f'First row mismatch: {first}'
    assert last == expected, f'Last row mismatch: {last}'"
    },
    {
      "name": "test_manhattan_diamond",
      "source": "def test_manhattan_diamond(run, x):
    n = int(x.strip())
    out = run(x)
    lines = out.strip('\n').split('\n')
    center = n // 2
    for i in range(n):
        for j in range(n):
            ch = lines[i][j]
            is_diamond = (abs(i - center) + abs(j - center) <= center)
            if is_diamond:
                assert ch == 'D', f'Cell ({i},{j}) should be D but is {ch}'
            else:
                assert ch == '*', f'Cell ({i},{j}) should be * but is {ch}'"
    }
  ]
}

